      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:3:3:31:5",
      "text": [
        " سَمِعْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) يَنْهَى عَنِ الْغُسْلِ إِذَا دَخَلَ الْقَبْرَ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Abu Ali Al Ashary, from Muhammad Bin Abdul Jabbar, from Al Hajjal, from Sa’alba, from Ma’amar Bin Yahya who said, ",
          "‘I heard Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> forbid from the washing, when entering the grave’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "5. Abu Ali al-Ash’ariy has narrated from Muhammad ibn ‘Abd al-Jabbar from al-Hajjal from Tha’labah from Mu’ammar ibn Yahya who has said the following: “I once heard abu ‘Abd Allah, Alayhi al-Salam, prohibit taking Ghusl (bath) because of entering the grave.” "
        ]
      }
    },
